WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.315
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.615 --> 00:00:08.607
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.907 --> 00:00:14.729
Unit nineteen: Basic Conjunctions (and/but/or). Today you will join ideas with and, but and or.

4
00:00:15.029 --> 00:00:17.704
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:21.644
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.483 --> 00:00:23.183
And.

7
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:26.636
And means a word that adds one idea to another.

8
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.041
I like tea and coffee.

9
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.641
Your turn. Say: And.

10
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.269
And.

11
00:00:36.017 --> 00:00:36.623
But.

12
00:00:37.617 --> 00:00:40.127
But means a word that shows a different idea.

13
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:42.647
I am tired, but I am happy.

14
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.345
Your turn. Say: But.

15
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:48.899
But.

16
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.500
Or.

17
00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.714
Or means a word that gives a choice.

18
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:55.898
Do you want tea or coffee?

19
00:00:56.483 --> 00:00:59.577
Your turn. Say: Or.

20
00:01:02.433 --> 00:01:03.040
Or.

21
00:01:03.783 --> 00:01:04.599
Connect.

22
00:01:05.583 --> 00:01:08.117
Connect means to join two things together.

23
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:10.589
Connect the two sentences.

24
00:01:11.183 --> 00:01:13.441
Your turn. Say: Connect.

25
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.197
Connect.

26
00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:18.777
Join.

27
00:01:19.783 --> 00:01:21.969
Join means to put things together.

28
00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:24.072
Join the two ideas.

29
00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:27.103
Your turn. Say: Join.

30
00:01:29.967 --> 00:01:30.770
Join.

31
00:01:31.517 --> 00:01:32.332
Choice.

32
00:01:33.317 --> 00:01:35.897
Choice means the act of choosing between things.

33
00:01:36.483 --> 00:01:37.728
You have a choice.

34
00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:40.830
Your turn. Say: Choice.

35
00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:44.610
Choice.

36
00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:46.398
Contrast.

37
00:01:47.383 --> 00:01:50.602
Contrast means a clear difference between two things.

38
00:01:51.217 --> 00:01:53.634
There is a contrast between hot and cold.

39
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:57.169
Your turn. Say: Contrast.

40
00:02:00.033 --> 00:02:01.058
Contrast.

41
00:02:01.817 --> 00:02:02.771
Addition.

42
00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:05.957
Addition means something that is added.

43
00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:07.946
And shows addition.

44
00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.935
Your turn. Say: Addition.

45
00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.720
Addition.

46
00:02:15.533 --> 00:02:19.056
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.917 --> 00:02:23.124
Visal, how can we join 'I like tea' and 'I like coffee'?

48
00:02:24.217 --> 00:02:34.999
We use and: I like tea and coffee. And adds one idea to another. We can also join two sentences: I play football and my sister dances.

49
00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:37.201
What about 'but'?

50
00:02:38.317 --> 00:02:48.463
But shows a contrast. I like tea, but I don't like coffee. It is small, but it is strong. Use a comma before but when it joins two sentences.

51
00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:50.423
And 'or'?

52
00:02:51.517 --> 00:03:02.043
Or gives a choice: Do you want tea or coffee? We can go by bus or by bike. We use and, but and or very often, so they are important words.

53
00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.735
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.583 --> 00:03:09.162
Grammar focus: Conjunctions: and and but and or.

55
00:03:09.462 --> 00:03:10.695
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.383 --> 00:03:13.371
I like tea and I like coffee.

57
00:03:14.283 --> 00:03:16.283
I am tired, but I am happy.

58
00:03:17.183 --> 00:03:18.707
Do you want tea or coffee?

59
00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:26.708
Use and to add, but to show a contrast and or to give a choice. Put a comma before but when it joins two sentences.

60
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.764
Be careful! Don't say: I am tired, or I am happy.

61
00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.501
Say: I am tired, but I am happy.

62
00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:37.498
Use but for a contrast.

63
00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.790
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.042
Joining Ideas.

65
00:03:43.342 --> 00:03:45.226
I like rice and fish for lunch.

66
00:03:46.233 --> 00:03:48.593
I am tired, but I want to study.

67
00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.692
Do you want to walk or ride a bike?

68
00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.605
We use and for addition and but for contrast.

69
00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.343
Or is for a choice, and it helps us decide.

70
00:04:00.433 --> 00:04:04.389
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.389
I like tea blank I don't like coffee.

72
00:04:07.689 --> 00:04:10.518
A, and. B, but. C, or.

73
00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.637
The answer is B: but.

74
00:04:16.783 --> 00:04:18.667
Do you want rice blank noodles?

75
00:04:18.967 --> 00:04:21.877
A, and. B, but. C, or.

76
00:04:25.433 --> 00:04:26.934
The answer is C: or.

77
00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:29.746
She is smart blank kind.

78
00:04:30.046 --> 00:04:32.875
A, and. B, but. C, or.

79
00:04:36.433 --> 00:04:38.282
The answer is A: and.

80
00:04:39.417 --> 00:04:41.126
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:41.426 --> 00:04:48.911
A, It is small, but it is strong.. B, It is small, or it is strong.. C, It is small, and but strong..

82
00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:55.534
The answer is A: It is small, but it is strong..

83
00:04:56.683 --> 00:04:59.484
According to the reading, which word is for a choice?

84
00:04:59.784 --> 00:05:03.031
A, or. B, and. C, but.

85
00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:08.311
The answer is A: or.

86
00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:12.756
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:13.617 --> 00:05:17.393
Write one sentence using 'and', one using 'but', and one using 'or'.

88
00:05:26.183 --> 00:05:27.788
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:28.088 --> 00:05:40.823
I like football and swimming. I am tired, but I want to play. Do you want tea or water? I use and to add ideas, but to show a different idea, and or to give a choice.

90
00:05:41.123 --> 00:05:42.867
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:43.783 --> 00:05:49.048
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and conjunctions: and and but and or.

92
00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:53.428
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

93
00:05:53.728 --> 00:05:56.590
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

94
00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:59.658
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

